<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Widget for the "Analyses" module.

    Route 1: it reads the off-vault reminder store that already exists so
    reminders can fire with the app shut, and shows what those reminders'
    notifications show — a generic title and a date. It works in every
    security mode. The labels the user typed appear only if this widget was
    given the same per-widget consent as mirrored content, and never in
    paranoid mode.

    Carries android:configure. The warning the original widget_info.xml records
    is about an *empty* configure attribute, which crashes the launcher on first
    add; a declared activity is fine, and per-instance configuration is what
    lets two widgets of the same module watch different things.

    Still updatePeriodMillis=0. Nothing here changes on a clock — the content is
    redrawn through WidgetRefresh whenever a reminder changes, and on every
    lock and unlock.
    Polling would wake the device forever to discover nothing.

    widgetFeatures="reconfigurable" (Android 9+, ignored before) lets a launcher
    offer the configuration again from the placed widget, so an opt-in can be
    given or withdrawn without removing and re-adding the card.

    No android:previewLayout: one the launcher cannot rasterise can crash the
    picker, and the system default preview is the safe choice.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="180dp"
    android:minHeight="110dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:targetCellHeight="3"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_content"
    android:configure="com.douxev.eggshell.widget.WidgetConfigActivity"
    android:widgetFeatures="reconfigurable"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:description="@string/widget_desc_labs"/>
